,"text":"Hit","abbreviation":"hit"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:03"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"22"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5238086","displayName":"Elias N. Pettersson","shortName":"Elias N. Pettersson"},"type":"hit-credited"},{"athlete":{"id":"4565257","displayName":"Bobby Brink","shortName":"B. Brink"},"type":"hitted"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1833","fullName":"Rogers Arena","address":{"city":"Vancouver","country":"Canada"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1833.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17560,"officials":[{"fullName":"Jordan Samuels-Thomas","displayName":"Jordan Samuels-Thomas","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Trent Knorr","displayName":"Trent Knorr","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Trevor Hanson","displayName":"Trevor Hanson","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jonathan Deschamps","displayName":"Jonathan Deschamps","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Quinn Hughes has a goal and an assist in his Vancouver return in Wild's 4-2 victory","description":"— Former Vancouver captain Quinn Hughes had a goal to reach 500 NHL points and added an assist in his return to Rogers Arena in the Minnesota Wild’s 4-2 victory over the Canucks on Sunday night.","story":"VANCOUVER, British Columbia -- — Former Vancouver captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4320548/quinn-hughes\">Quinn Hughes</a> had a goal to reach 500 NHL points and added an assist in his return to Rogers Arena in the Minnesota Wild’s 4-2 victory over the Canucks on Sunday night.\n\n\r\n              Traded to Minnesota in December, Hughes was booed throughout the night.\n\n\r\n              He scored on a power player midway through the second period to make it 3-0, and set up Kirill Kaprizov’s NHL-leading 13th goal early in the third for a 4-0 advantage. In 13 games this season, Hughes has three goals and 13 assists.\n\n\r\n              Picked seventh overall by the Canucks in 2018, Hughes played 6 1/2 seasons in Vancouver before the blockbuster trade sent him to Minnesota. The deal saw Vancouver acquire <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697391/marco-rossi\">Marco Rossi</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080163/liam-ohgren\">Liam Ohgren</a>, defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5206642/zeev-buium\">Zeev Buium</a> and the Wild’s first-round pick in the 2026 NHL draft.\n\n\r\n              Kaprizov and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5302535/maxim-shabanov\">Maxim Shabanov</a> also each had a goal and assist, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565257/bobby-brink\">Bobby Brink</a> scored.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5524/calvin-pickard\">Calvin Pickard</a> made 15 saves as the Wild improved to 8-3-2, following up a 5-1 victory over the Kraken in Seattle on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4996099/max-sasson\">Max Sasson</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899979/brock-boeser\">Brock Boeser</a> scored for Vancouver. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4894703/leevi-merilainen\">Leevi Merilainen</a> stopped 30 shots.\n\n\r\n              Vancouver dropped to 2-10-1 with its 10th straight loss.\n\n\r\n              Hughes became the second-fastest American defenseman to reach 500 NHL points, achieving the feat in 520 games. Brian Leetch hit the milestone in 496 games with the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a>.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              <hl2 />\r\n              Wild: At Utah on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Canucks: At Anaheim on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-26T04:56:01Z"}}